title: Party Demands
subtitle: Stegerwald's position is not yet secure...
view-if: year = 1929 and month = 1
new-page: true

= Party Demands
  
While Stegerwald has been elected party chariman, his position is still very fragile. In his ambitious inaguration speech, He vowed to transform the Center into the main party of the German right, affirming commitments to the 1920 Essen Program. the Center is concerned that eroding the pragmatic nature of the party in favor of interconfessionalism and worker's rights wil cause great instability, the clerical wing claims that the party is abandoning Catholicism and that the party's role as protector of the Catholic faith far outweighs whtatever electoral gains will be made. The Unions are already growing impatient, expecting expansion of welfare and worker's rights. In short, if Stegerwald fails to deliver until the 1930 Party Congress, his downfall is all but assured.

